  "b6_reason": "Metals have a positive temperature coefficient (more lattice scattering), while semiconductors have a negative one (many more charge carriers are thermally generated).",
  "b6_working": "Conductors: carrier concentration is fixed, rising temperature increases electron-phonon collisions, relaxation time falls, so resistance rises. Semiconductors: thermal excitation across the gap increases n exponentially, which outweighs the mobility fall, so resistance drops.",
